  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for conflict prevention in the Savane region for inclusive and sustainable management of natural resources and the promotion of communitysecurity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Togo, like the coastal countries of West Africa, is not spared from the harmful effects of the security crisis in the Sahel region. Conflicts in neighboring countries have facilitated the infiltration of extremist and terrorist groups into northern Togo, particularly in the Savanes region, where incursions and attacks against security forces have increased. This situation is exacerbated by the proximity of the region to Benin&apos;s Pendjari (W) Park and the Central East region of Burkina Faso, areas where terrorist groups frequently operate. This context of security instability, violent extremism, organized cross border trafficking, and broader geopolitical pressures is producing severe consequences for local populations. The influx of refugees and internally displaced persons is placing additional strain on natural resources such as water, land, and forests, already heavily affected by climate change. The Savanes region was already the most vulnerable region prior to the crisis. Poverty remains extremely high (63.9% in 2021). Youth are particularly affected with unemployment and labor underutilization highest in the country (25.6%), with at least 30% of young people neither employed nor in education/training. The project aims to address interconnected security, socio economic, and resilience challenges to support inclusive and sustainable development in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
